# THE PLAYTEST MAP. Not a test fixture -- the tests keep their own segments
# (test_flat, test_ascent) so that tuning this one for feel can never break the
# gate, and the gate can never constrain what this one is allowed to be.
#
# 15 cells (30 m) across. Wide enough for a party to spread out and for a plinko
# field to have lanes, narrow enough that a shove crosses most of it and you can
# always see what your friends are doing.
#
# TWO REAL STEPS, height 0 -> 2 -> 4, so the climb repeats rather than happening
# once. Each step offers all three ascenders side by side, which is the point of
# the first half of the map: a group can compare them in one walk.
#
#   x 1-2    GENTLE ramp  -- 1 height unit per cell (~27 deg). Walkable alone.
#   x 7-8    STEEP ramp   -- 2 units per cell (45 deg). Above max_walk_slope, so
#                            no single-player solution: shove or rope.
#   x 12-13  LADDER       -- free, the ordinary case. NOT CLIMBABLE YET: the
#                            glyph validates and the loader collects it, but
#                            there is no climb mechanic, so today it is a 2 m
#                            wall. The gentle ramp is the working route.
#
# Rows 7 and 13 are the cliffs: everything that is not an ascender is a hole, so
# the deck above can ONLY be entered through one of the three.
#
# The walk:
#   z 0-1    flat entry, two pillars to shove around
#   z 2-3    a gap to walk past
#   z 4-5    NO PARAPET on both sides -- the exposed run
#   z 6-7    first ascent, to height 2
#   z 8-11   middle deck, two gaps and pillars
#   z 12-13  second ascent, to height 4
#   z 14-15  upper deck, a pillar cluster
#   z 16-17  WATER channel across the middle (geometry only until M7)
#   z 18-27  THE PLINKO ARENA -- see below
#   z 28-29  the run out
#
# HATS (`^`) at z4 (x3, x11) and z24 (x2, x12).
#
# SPECIALS. Machine guns (`*`) at z12 and z18, both on the centre line where the
# party is already walking. GRENADES (`g`) are placed the other way round, because
# the two weapons want different things from the player: one at z15 tucked inside
# the upper pillar cluster, and one at z20 out on the parapet-less side of the
# plinko arena. Both are a step off the route and one of them is a step toward the
# drop, which is the trade a thrown weapon should be asking for.
#
# MINES (`x`) at z9 and z25, and both are placed to be USED where they are found
# rather than carried. z9 is the middle deck between two gaps, a few cells short of
# the second ascent -- a natural place to want something waiting behind you. z25 is
# between the last mound pair and the shooters, which is the one stretch of this
# map where the party knows what is coming and has a moment to prepare for it.
# That moment is the whole reason a mine exists.
#
# PAST A HAZARD, NOT BESIDE THE SAFE SPOT, which is the whole authoring rule for
# them. The z6 pair sit out on the exposed no-parapet run, right where the z5
# rushers wake -- so collecting one means standing in the worst place on the
# bridge while something runs at you. The z24 pair are deep in the plinko arena,
# in the pillar lanes, where the balls are.
#
# Both are also placed so that being knocked off while wearing them scatters the
# stack somewhere awkward, which is the joke.
#
# RUSHER MOUNDS (`m`) at z5, z10, z14 and z26. The first one is at z5 and not
# earlier on purpose: spawn is z1 and the trigger radius is 3 cells, so anything
# at z3 or nearer would wake before anybody had taken a step, and the telegraph
# would play to an audience that had not started watching yet.
#
# Placed on OPEN ROWS, never inside the pillar clusters. A rusher runs in a
# straight line and only chases what it can see, so a mound with a pillar in
# front of it is a mound that mostly never fires. The pair at z5 is the intended
# first encounter: that stretch has no parapet on either side, so the thing
# chasing you and the thing that makes being chased matter are in the same place.
#
# THE PLINKO ARENA (z 19-27). A staggered field, offset every other row so a
# ball never has a straight lane to fall down -- that stagger is what makes the
# scatter, and it is why the pillars are cylinders (a box would jam a ball in a
# corner and a stuck ball is a dead ball). Three shooters sit at the TOP of the
# field, up-bridge of it, so their output travels back down at the party under
# the bridge's own 4-degree pitch.
#
# The parapet is suppressed down both sides of the middle of the arena. That is
# the danger: a ball does not have to kill you, it only has to knock you
# sideways while you are standing somewhere with nothing to stop you.

name = playtest_bridge
base_height = 0
width = 15
length = 30
tags = foot, playtest, ramp, ladder, water, plinko, two_step

